WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.230
-: I can also use git diff

00:01.230 --> 00:03.870
to compare changes between two branches.

00:03.870 --> 00:06.330
So if I have two branches, currently I don't

00:06.330 --> 00:09.720
in the repo I was showing you, but whatever branch one is

00:09.720 --> 00:12.390
and branch two are, Git will do a diff

00:12.390 --> 00:14.460
between the files in those branches,

00:14.460 --> 00:16.513
so all the files in those branches,

00:16.513 --> 00:18.930
although you can narrow it down as well.

00:18.930 --> 00:21.120
So let's do a quick demo of that.

00:21.120 --> 00:25.860
I need to make a branch, so why don't I commit the changes.

00:25.860 --> 00:27.600
I added, what, Indigo and Vie,

00:27.600 --> 00:30.960
or I added Violet, and I added my Numbers file.

00:30.960 --> 00:35.960
Let's just go with "add violet and create numbers,"

00:36.930 --> 00:38.580
and then I'll add a couple of numbers here,

00:38.580 --> 00:43.350
one, two, three, four, git status.

00:43.350 --> 00:48.350
Let's do, clear this, git commit -am "add more numbers."

00:54.570 --> 00:57.420
Alrighty, and now, if I make a branch,

00:57.420 --> 01:00.960
so I'm gonna create a new branch, git switch -c,

01:00.960 --> 01:04.203
we'll call this branch, how about odd-numbers?

01:05.490 --> 01:08.700
So on this branch, I'm only going to have odd numbers,

01:08.700 --> 01:13.290
so I'm gonna delete two and I'll delete four,

01:13.290 --> 01:18.290
I'll do a commit, so I'll add numbers, then I'll commit,

01:18.727 --> 01:22.920
"removed two and four," okay, and then let's

01:22.920 --> 01:24.783
also add five down at the bottom,

01:25.890 --> 01:30.890
so we'll do a git add numbers, git commit "add five."

01:33.150 --> 01:36.720
Okay, so right now, we have two branches,

01:36.720 --> 01:40.140
nothing very exciting, but we have master and odd numbers,

01:40.140 --> 01:42.300
and if I wanna do a comparison between the two

01:42.300 --> 01:44.250
of them, I wanna see what has changed

01:44.250 --> 01:46.980
from master to odd numbers or vice versa,

01:46.980 --> 01:49.980
the order does matter, but I list the two branches

01:49.980 --> 01:51.840
and I separate them by two dots,

01:51.840 --> 01:54.048
or you can actually just add a space.

01:54.048 --> 01:56.820
Both of them will do the same thing.

01:56.820 --> 02:00.510
So let's do, which, let's do from master

02:00.510 --> 02:05.510
to odd numbers first, so git diff master..odd-numbers,

02:08.550 --> 02:12.030
and the only file that changed was Numbers.

02:12.030 --> 02:14.400
We still have the Colors file on both branches,

02:14.400 --> 02:17.250
but there's no differences, so there's nothing to display.

02:17.250 --> 02:21.090
Now here, we can see that numbers.txt version A,

02:21.090 --> 02:23.040
which is from the master branch,

02:23.040 --> 02:26.193
because of that order that I wrote, master to odd numbers,

02:27.060 --> 02:28.740
this one is from the master branch

02:28.740 --> 02:31.110
and this one is from my odd numbers branch,

02:31.110 --> 02:32.910
so we see that on the master branch,

02:32.910 --> 02:34.620
which is, A, it has the minus sign

02:34.620 --> 02:37.650
in front of it, that's its designated symbol.

02:37.650 --> 02:40.770
We had one, two, three, four,

02:40.770 --> 02:43.322
and we did not have this stuff, right?

02:43.322 --> 02:48.030
Then on B, we have the plus sign as its symbol,

02:48.030 --> 02:51.450
so we had one, three, and then five.

02:51.450 --> 02:54.720
So that's new on the odd numbers branch

02:54.720 --> 02:57.180
and it does not include two and four.

02:57.180 --> 03:02.180
If I change the order, git diff odd-numbers and then master,

03:04.560 --> 03:06.000
now, we see things have flipped,

03:06.000 --> 03:08.250
so A has been assigned the minus sign,

03:08.250 --> 03:13.250
but A this time is the odd numbers branch and B is master.

03:13.800 --> 03:17.370
So here, right on the master branch, B with a plus sign,

03:17.370 --> 03:19.800
we have one, two, three, four,

03:19.800 --> 03:22.140
and it's the opposite of what we saw previously,

03:22.140 --> 03:24.030
so that order does matter.

03:24.030 --> 03:27.600
Also, just to make this clear, we get the same outcome

03:27.600 --> 03:31.440
if we just use a space, but people like to use the dot, dot.

03:31.440 --> 03:34.260
Maybe it makes it, I don't know, makes it clearer,

03:34.260 --> 03:35.970
you know, that you're doing that comparison,

03:35.970 --> 03:38.490
but you'll see both of them, and then,

03:38.490 --> 03:41.040
let me just quickly change one of these files.

03:41.040 --> 03:44.070
So let's do red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo,

03:44.070 --> 03:46.170
violet, I don't know, odd numbers?

03:46.170 --> 03:49.110
We'll only display the odd-numbered colors,

03:49.110 --> 03:51.630
so if this is one, get rid of two.

03:51.630 --> 03:55.294
That's three, we get rid of four, five, and six.

03:55.294 --> 03:57.690
I dunno, I might've totally screwed that up, but whatever.

03:57.690 --> 03:59.670
We have fewer colors here.

03:59.670 --> 04:03.390
So now, we type git status. Let's make a commit here.

04:03.390 --> 04:05.280
So I'll add the Colors file

04:05.280 --> 04:09.090
and we'll just go with "remove some colors," alright?

04:09.090 --> 04:10.800
So now, if I do a git diff, let's go

04:10.800 --> 04:12.813
from master to odd numbers again,

04:14.520 --> 04:16.830
we have two files that are showing up.

04:16.830 --> 04:18.570
So the Colors file changed

04:18.570 --> 04:21.060
from master to odd numbers, right?

04:21.060 --> 04:24.960
On master, which is A, we had orange, green, and indigo.

04:24.960 --> 04:27.360
They are not present on the odd numbers branch

04:27.360 --> 04:30.330
and we didn't add anything new, but on the Numbers file,

04:30.330 --> 04:32.010
we have the same thing we saw earlier.

04:32.010 --> 04:33.810
We don't need to go over it again.

04:33.810 --> 04:36.450
So now, we have multiple files because there were changes

04:36.450 --> 04:38.820
to multiple files between those branches.

04:38.820 --> 04:40.260
So that's how you compare branches

04:40.260 --> 04:44.763
with git diff, dot dot, or a space between two branch names.
